<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">West Ukrainian People's Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1919 CE · capital Lviv</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ukrainian state of eastern Galicia, proclaimed in Lviv in 1918, which fought Poland and briefly united with the Ukrainian People's Republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> collapsed, Ukrainian soldiers seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> on 1 November 1918, and a Ukrainian National Council proclaimed the West <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic">Ukrainian People's Republic</a> over eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-galicia-and-lodomeria">Galicia</a>, northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bukovina">Bukovina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-ruthenia">Transcarpathia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yevhen-petrushevych">Yevhen Petrushevych</a> became its president and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kost-levytsky">Kost Levytsky</a> headed the government.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic quickly built a working administration, police and courts out of former Austrian institutions and formed the disciplined Ukrainian Galician Army. Polish residents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> resisted, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-ukrainian-war">Polish-Ukrainian War</a> began; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukrainians">Ukrainians</a> lost Lviv in November and moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ternopil">Ternopil</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivano-frankivsk">Stanislaviv</a>. In January 1919 the republic proclaimed union with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic">Ukrainian People's Republic</a>, keeping its own government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A Polish offensive in mid 1919 drove the Galician Army across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zbruch-river">Zbruch</a> in July, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-polish-republic">Second Polish Republic</a> occupied the whole territory. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yevhen-petrushevych">Petrushevych</a>'s government went into exile, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> recognised Polish rule over eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-galicia-and-lodomeria">Galicia</a> in 1923.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/west-ukrainian-peoples-republic.jpg" alt="West Ukrainian People's Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: Ιγκόρ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ukraine_(1917%E2%80%931921).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lviv</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yevhen Petrushevych, Kost Levytsky</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ukrainian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>ZUNR, Western Ukrainian People's Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=west-ukrainian-peoples-republic" aria-label="West Ukrainian People's Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5231 443 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where West Ukrainian People's Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5551 699L5508 714M5551 699L5380 747M5551 699L5697 681M5551 699L5473 630"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5508 714h0M5380 747h0M5697 681h0M5473 630h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5551 699h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5551 699h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lviv. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=west-ukrainian-peoples-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
